## §Rows skipped, with reason
a#4  003 sentencing hedge (3/4/6 months). SKIPPED as written. RULEBOOK-FIX R3 explicitly requires the hedge the reviewer wants removed: «003 "courts currently impose about 3 months" → "in some judgments about 3 months has been imposed; there is no typical or guaranteed outcome"», and ACCEPTED-ROUND forbids making a result sentence positive. Only the Persian was made more idiomatic inside the hedge («… حدود 3 ماه حبس تعیین شده است؛ هیچ کیفر نوعی یا نتیجهٔ تضمین‌شده‌ای در کار نیست.»). See "reviewer got it wrong" below.
a#6  003 re-adding «بیشترین» ("maximum compensation"). SKIPPED. R3 requires exactly the opposite: «"pursue the maximum / highest possible compensation" → "pursue the compensation the facts and evidence support"». Advertising-rule row.
a#7  008 «B غرامت اخراج قابل‌توجهی دریافت کرد». SKIPPED. R3 requires «with legal representation was able to establish the entitlement under the law», which is what the file already says; ACCEPTED-fa a#6 (round 2) pinned that wording. Only the following clause was polished («چنین ادله‌ای در اختیار نداشتند»).
a#27 003 Q16–Q20 as «## Q…» headings, removal of U+200B lines and of the empty `**​**` bold lines in 005. SKIPPED — structural, pinned by the checker against the Korean source:
       · `checkHeadings` compares the full heading-level vector with the source; the source has Q16–Q20 as plain body lines (src/content/columns/003…md lines 198/234/258/278/298), so adding five `##` headings fails the check.
       · `checkBlocks` compares the ZWSP count with the source. Measured source vs fa: 003 52/52, 005 8/8, 006 4/4, 008 10/10, 009 5/5, 013 5/5, 015 3/3 — the U+200B lines and the `**​**` blocks are in the Korean source, and removing them fails both `blocks` and `ZWSP`.
       ACCEPTED-ROUND also lists "requests to merge/split paragraphs, headings … or to add new headings" as skip.
b#11 013/015 U+200B removal. SKIPPED for the same reason (source-pinned ZWSP count).
a#31 pack «TWD 1.57M». The reformat itself is a documented skip (ACCEPTED-ROUND: "keep byte-identical — a test pins it"). Applied the pattern the `my` locale already uses instead: «حکم بدوی به پرداخت 1.57 میلیون دلار جدید تایوان (TWD 1.57M) صادر شد.» — the pinned token is untouched byte-for-byte and the Persian reading is added beside it. Full suite re-run after the change: 3202/3202 pass.
Frontmatter `url:` with Hangul in 008/009 — skipped (R16, canonical source metadata).

## §Checker constraints noted (WO: "prefer the form the checker accepts and note it")
The fa entry of `WORD_NUMERAL_LEXICONS` (scripts/check-column-translation.mjs, `SMALL_LEXICON_WORDS`) parses only یک=1, دو=2, سه=3 (and اول/یکم/دوم/سوم). Spelling out any other digit deletes a number the Korean source carries and makes `numbers` FAIL ("missing from translation"). So:
 · a#26 «پنج سال پیاپی» — NOT applied; 5 kept as a digit in 001 (اقامت دائم) — پنج is not in the lexicon.
 · b#13 «اخطار سی‌روزه» — written «اخطار 30 روزه»; سی is not in the lexicon.
 · b#21 «مدت عمومی شش‌ماهه» — written «مدت عمومی 6 ماهه»; شش is not in the lexicon. «سه ماهه» would parse but the pair was kept in one style for readability.
 · Sentencing/statutory figures (003 «3 ماه / 4 ماه / 6 ماه», 006 «3 سال / 5 سال», 007 grounds-for-divorce list, 014 notice-period table, 011 «3 سال / 3 ماه», 016 «3 ماه») kept as digits — the reviewer's own rule exempts tables and statutory citations, and it keeps number parity robust.
 · b#1 «دو سوم» without the «(2/3)» parenthetical was verified against the checker before being kept: 018 numbers PASS sourceCount=25 targetCount=25. 002 keeps its existing «دو سوم (2/3)» form, which part a did not flag.
Test edit: `src/data/__tests__/guidance-disclosure-parity.test.ts` fa markers widened to match the a#28 rewording — `/تعهد به نتیجه/` → `/تعهدی? به نتیجه/` and `/مهلت پاسخ/` → `/مهلتی? (?:برای )?پاسخ/` (ACCEPTED-ROUND "Disclosure parity" clause). Nothing else in tests was touched.
009-taiwan-voluntary-resignation-severance.md has no r5 findings and no systemic hits; left unmodified.

## §Things I believe the reviewer got wrong (NOT applied)
1. fa-a a#4 — "«در برخی احکام» downgrades the usual sentence to an occasional one". That downgrade is deliberate: RULEBOOK-FIX R3 orders it for 003 in every locale (Taiwan attorney advertising rules — no typical-outcome claim). Reverting to «دادگاه‌ها … عموماً … حکم می‌کنند» would re-introduce the claim the campaign is removing.
2. fa-a a#6 — "«maximum» was lost". It was removed on purpose by R3 ("pursue the compensation the facts and evidence support"). Re-adding «بیشترین» is a result/superlative claim.
3. fa-a a#7 — "the Persian stops at proving entitlement". That is the R3 replacement for the original "obtained a high severance" anecdote, and ACCEPTED-fa a#6 pinned it in round 2. The reviewer's suggested text restores a result claim ("غرامت اخراج قابل‌توجهی دریافت کرد").
4. fa-a a#27 / fa-b b#11 — the U+200B lines, the `**​**` blocks and the Q16–Q20 body lines are not translation defects: they are present in the Korean source and are pinned byte-for-byte by the checker's `blocks`/`ZWSP`/`headings` checks. Fixing them belongs to the source file, not to the Persian.
5. fa-a a#31 — "TWD 1.57M … the currency code precedes the amount". The token is test-pinned; see above for how it was handled without touching the token.
6. fa-b b#32's wider claim that «خواندن» is always wrong for "match": «با هم می‌خوانند / با مدارک عینی نمی‌خواند» is idiomatic Persian and was kept where it reads naturally (002, 004); only the comparative «بهتر می‌خواند تا …» and «با شرکت‌هایی می‌خواند که …» constructions were rewritten.

